# CODEOWNERS — required review for privileged CI configuration (Issue #208)
#
# This repository ships privileged workflows:
#   - .github/workflows/wasm-bundle.yml  — id-token: write (OIDC keyless Sigstore signing)
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml, upgrade-dependencies.yml — secrets.ACTIONS_PUSH (PAT, contents:write)
#   - .github/workflows/semgrep.yml      — secrets.SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN
#
# A change to any of these runs with those secrets / the OIDC token. Requiring
# a designated owner to review edits to the CI configuration closes the path
# where a single self-approved pull request quietly exfiltrates a secret or
# mints a signed artefact. These rules only take effect once the default
# branch (Develop) enables "Require review from Code Owners" — see
# docs/archive/pr-summaries/pr-summary-208.md for the branch-protection steps.
#
# Owners are named as concrete org members (repo admins) rather than a team:
# the org has no `maintainers` team and no team holds explicit write access to
# this repo, so a team entry would be an invalid, silently-unenforced owner.
# Swap these for a team (e.g. @stSoftwareAU/<team>) once such a team exists and
# is granted write access.

# Privileged CI: workflows and any composite/local actions.
/.github/workflows/   @Green-Beret @nleck
/.github/actions/     @Green-Beret @nleck

# Protect this ownership map itself from unreviewed edits.
/.github/CODEOWNERS    @Green-Beret @nleck
